# Scope: the school's SELF-TOP-UP WALLET (SchoolBalance) and its ledger (SchoolBalanceEntry).
#
# It does NOT hold the quota that comes with a plan -- that is SchoolSubscriptionQuotaRecord in
# subscription.graphqls, a completely different pocket: split by QuotaType, re-issued every period,
# and its used amount is always clamped at total. This wallet is ONE number, lives across periods,
# and is only charged once the quota of the matching type is exhausted.
#
# The debt log (SchoolDebtEvent) is also here, moved over from school.graphqls: debt is the flip side of
# this very wallet -- a negative balance IS the debt -- so the two ledgers must be read in one place.
# They answer two different questions about the same wallet: the statement says "where did the money
# go", the debt log says "why is the school locked".
#
# MONEY IN THIS FILE IS String, NOT Float -- an intentional deviation from the common convention.
# The Float convention written at the top of subscription.graphqls rests on one premise: "VND is
# always whole, numeric(15,0) stays below 2^53 so a JS client reads it without losing precision".
# That premise is NOT true here: school_balances.balance_vnd and school_balance_entries.amount_vnd are
# numeric(18,6), deliberately keeping 6 decimal places because one practice session can cost only a
# few hundredths of a dong (see the column comment in V2). 128440.95 cannot be represented exactly as
# a double, and this is exactly the place where the numbers must match absolutely: the ledger
# invariant is SUM(amount_vnd) = balance_vnd.
#
# The returned value is the COMPLETE decimal string built by BigDecimal.toPlainString() -- no
# scientific notation, no thousands separators, keeping the stored scale ("-128440.950000"). Clients
# parse it with a decimal library or Number() for display, and must never add up amountVnd to rebuild
# the balance: balanceAfterVnd is stored precisely so that nobody has to add up.
#
# When the project moves all 24 schemas to a BigDecimal scalar, this is the group of fields that
# changes first, and these Strings disappear at the same time.

enum SchoolBalanceEntryType {
    "The school tops up the wallet -- always tied to an order that has been fully paid."
    TOP_UP
    """
    Deducts the part of the AI cost that EXCEEDS the quota that comes with the plan. The part that is
    still within the quota is NOT recorded here -- it is already counted in
    school_subscription_quota_records.used_amount_vnd, and recording it again would count the same
    dong twice. That is why the sum of this ledger's amount column is NOT the school's total AI cost.
    """
    OVERAGE_CHARGE
    """
    The school moves money from the self-top-up wallet into the QUOTA wallet of one quota type. The
    money LEAVES the wallet but is NOT an AI expense -- it goes to another pocket of the same school, so
    it has no costUsd/fxRateUsed and is not tied to any session. quotaType and actorId are mandatory (V12).

    ONE-WAY and currently not undoable: no transfer back to the wallet, no transfer to the other quota
    type, and an ADJUSTMENT row is NOT a way to fix it. See FundQuotaFromBalanceUseCase.
    """
    QUOTA_FUNDING
    "A refund -- always tied to the original order."
    REFUND
    "A manual correction by the system admin. The person who did it and the reason are mandatory."
    ADJUSTMENT
}

"""
The school's SELF-TOP-UP wallet. It lives across every renewal/plan change and never expires.

It is NOT "the remaining quota". The wallet is only charged WHEN the quota that comes with the plan
for the matching type is exhausted -- merging the two numbers into one silently erases the per-type
limit.
"""
type SchoolBalance {
    schoolId: ID!
    "Negative = in debt. The DB column intentionally has no CHECK >= 0 -- the negative part IS the debt."
    balanceVnd: String!
    """
    balanceVnd < 0. Returned ready-made instead of letting the client compare with 0: this is exactly
    the rule SchoolSubscriptionDebtGuardService uses to block opening an assessment session and
    entering one with an OTP, and a rule should be defined in only one place. It is also the right
    home for isLocked -- the field that was removed from SchoolSubscriptionQuotaRecord because the lock
    is a SCHOOL-level fact, not a property of each quota wallet.
    """
    locked: Boolean!
    "null when the school has never touched the wallet."
    updatedAt: DateTime
}

"""
One entry of the wallet ledger. Append-only: no edits, no deletes, no mutation at all.
"""
type SchoolBalanceEntry {
    id: ID!
    schoolId: ID!
    entryType: SchoolBalanceEntryType!
    "Positive = top-up / refund / upward adjustment. Negative = deduction."
    amountVnd: String!
    """
    The balance RIGHT AFTER this entry, taken as the stored value.

    Build a statement by reading this column, not by adding up amountVnd: the ledger is paginated, so
    adding up over one page gives a wrong number from the very first row of the second page.
    """
    balanceAfterVnd: String!
    occurredAt: DateTime!

    "The subscription period that was running when this happened. For tracing ONLY -- the balance does not belong to any plan."
    subscriptionId: ID

    # Source. Which field has a value is decided by entryType, and the DB already has a CHECK that
    # enforces exactly that combination. The client branches on entryType, not on "which other field
    # is not null".

    "TOP_UP, REFUND."
    orderId: ID
    "OVERAGE_CHARGE. EXACTLY ONE of the two session fields has a value."
    assessmentSessionId: ID
    "OVERAGE_CHARGE. EXACTLY ONE of the two session fields has a value."
    practiceSessionId: ID
    """
    OVERAGE_CHARGE: the quota wallet that pushed this amount over -- the REPORTING direction, not a
    separate wallet.
    QUOTA_FUNDING: the quota wallet the money has just GONE INTO -- the opposite direction, and
    information that cannot be derived from anywhere else on the row. Mandatory for both types.
    """
    quotaType: QuotaType
    "OVERAGE_CHARGE. The ORIGINAL cost computed by the provider. Kept in USD to reconcile back against the Azure invoice."
    costUsd: String
    """
    OVERAGE_CHARGE. The exchange rate LOCKED at the time of the charge, not today's rate -- and the
    weighted average over the whole session, so costUsd * fxRateUsed matches the amountVnd of this very
    entry exactly. Taking the rate of a single call would make the back-reconciliation come out wrong.
    """
    fxRateUsed: String
    "ADJUSTMENT: mandatory. REFUND, QUOTA_FUNDING: may be present."
    reason: String
    """
    ADJUSTMENT: the SYSTEM admin made a manual correction. QUOTA_FUNDING: the SCHOOL admin pressed
    top-up. null for every other type -- they are written by the system, not by anyone pressing a
    button. The two roles differ, so the client must branch on entryType to pick the label, rather
    than reading only actorId != null.

    A raw id rather than a name, the same way SchoolDebtEvent returns triggerAssessmentSessionId: showing
    the name needs a LEFT JOIN to users, and then the DTO can no longer be built from the domain model
    alone. Worth doing when a real screen needs it, not something to prepare in advance.
    """
    actorId: ID
}

type SchoolBalanceEntryPage {
    content: [SchoolBalanceEntry!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
}

"""
Totals over a TIME RANGE, computed in the DB.

It cannot be built on the client: the client holds only one page of 20 rows, while the range to add up
can be thousands. It is also the source of the "Deducted in the last 30 days" figure on the wallet
balance page.
"""
type SchoolBalanceSummary {
    "TOP_UP + REFUND. Always >= 0."
    creditedVnd: String!
    "OVERAGE_CHARGE. Always <= 0."
    overageChargedVnd: String!
    """
    QUOTA_FUNDING. Always <= 0.

    A SEPARATE group, not merged into overageChargedVnd even though the sign is the same: this amount
    is NOT money that has been spent, it is still the school's money, only sitting in the quota wallet
    instead of the self-top-up wallet. Merging the two would tell the principal that the school has
    spent an amount it never spent.

    It is here because these four groups must explain EVERY change of the balance within the range.
    If any group is missing, the statement shows a wallet that dropped with no total cell saying why --
    exactly the place where a reconciliation ledger must not stay silent.
    """
    quotaFundedVnd: String!
    "ADJUSTMENT. Either sign is possible."
    adjustedVnd: String!
}

# =============================================================================================
# The AI quota debt log, moved over from school.graphqls.
#
# Four money columns changed from Float to String at the same time as the file move, for exactly the
# same reason as the ledger above: school_debt_events is also numeric(18,6). Keeping Float here would
# make the two ledgers describe the SAME debt with two different types, and the debt figure on the log
# would not match the balance on the statement exactly -- precisely where a reconciliation ledger must
# not drift.
#
# This IS a breaking contract change, safe only because there is currently no caller: the query has
# been runnable for a long time but no screen uses it. Changing it now is the cheapest; once the Debt
# Log page goes live it no longer is.
# =============================================================================================

enum SchoolDebtEventType {
    LOCKED
    CAP_EXCEEDED
    CLEARED
}

"""
The audit ledger "cause of AI quota debt" -- each row is exactly 1 quota bucket of the school that has
just changed state (over the quota / over the warning ceiling / debt cleared), together with the
session and the VND amount that caused that transition.
See SchoolDebtEvent (domain model) / SchoolDebtNotificationService.

Written only on a state CHANGE, not on every deduction: a gap between two rows does not mean the
debt has stopped. And an empty ledger is a NORMAL state -- a school that regularly spends beyond its
quota but whose wallet always stays positive produces no rows.
"""
type SchoolDebtEvent {
    id: ID!
    schoolId: ID!
    # The name subscriptionId is kept ON PURPOSE: this column holds the id of the SUBSCRIPTION, even
    # though the domain model names the field subscriptionPlanId. The model is the wrong side; do not
    # rename it here before the model is fixed, otherwise it would have to be renamed twice in
    # opposite directions.
    subscriptionId: ID!
    eventType: SchoolDebtEventType!
    """
    null for CLEARED: clearing the debt is a SCHOOL-level event. The balance is ONE number shared by
    both quota wallets, so "which wallet just cleared its debt" has no answer -- inventing a value to
    fill the gap would dirty the very book used for reconciliation. See
    chk_school_debt_events_shape_matches_event_type.
    """
    quotaType: QuotaType
    "LOCKED/CAP_EXCEEDED: EXACTLY ONE of the two session fields has a value. CLEARED: both are null."
    triggerAssessmentSessionId: ID
    triggerPracticeSessionId: ID
    # The four columns below were renamed from ...Usd to VND at the same time as school_debt_events
    # (V2 section 15) and SchoolDebtEventDto: every number that comes in here is already in VND from
    # ConsumeQuotaService, and keeping the Usd suffix would only make the client misread the unit of an
    # amount of money.
    #
    # String, not Float -- same reason as the ledger above, see the comment block at the top of the file.
    "null for a CLEARED row: clearing the debt is not caused by any single deduction."
    triggerAmountVnd: String
    "null for CLEARED, same reason as quotaType."
    totalAllocatedVnd: String
    # NOT a value read from the quota record, but a figure REBUILT as totalAllocated + debt. The real
    # record is always clamped at exactly the quota (the excess was pushed to the wallet), so copying it
    # here would make every row show "used = quota, debt = 0" -- see the javadoc of
    # publishSchoolLockedDueToDebt.
    usedAmountVnd: String
    "The debt at that moment. Always 0 for a CLEARED row, by the very definition of cleared."
    overageVnd: String!
    occurredAt: DateTime
}

type SchoolDebtEventPage {
    content: [SchoolDebtEvent!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
}

extend type Query {
    """
    The wallet of one school. A SCHOOL_ADMIN can only read their own school, a SYSTEM_ADMIN can read
    every school -- the same check as schoolDebtEvents.

    NOT null: a school that has never touched the wallet receives a 0-dong copy built on the spot. The
    balance row is created lazily (only the first time the wallet is touched), and an empty wallet and a
    0-dong wallet mean the same thing -- see SchoolBalance.emptyFor. Returning null here would only make
    the client add a branch for the same state.
    """
    schoolBalance(schoolId: ID!): SchoolBalance!

    "The wallet statement, newest first. Leave entryType empty to not filter by type."
    schoolBalanceEntries(
        schoolId: ID!,
        entryType: SchoolBalanceEntryType,
        page: Int! = 1,
        size: Int! = 20
    ): SchoolBalanceEntryPage!

    """
    Totals over a time range. from/to are DateTime values (for example "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"); leave
    one empty to leave that end unbounded.

    to is NOT inclusive: two adjacent ranges (July ending 01/08, August starting 01/08) would count an
    entry that falls exactly on the boundary twice if <= were used.
    """
    schoolBalanceSummary(schoolId: ID!, from: DateTime, to: DateTime): SchoolBalanceSummary!

    """
    The quota debt log. The same permission check as the three queries above.

    The signature is kept EXACTLY as it was in school.graphqls (page/size are nullable Int, not Int!) --
    moving the file and changing the money type is already enough for one step, there is no need to add
    one more difference to remember.
    """
    schoolDebtEvents(schoolId: ID!, page: Int = 1, size: Int = 20): SchoolDebtEventPage!
}
